         15.9% of the text width; row 1's portraits total 31.5% against row 2's 36%, so
         row 1 carries the wider right margin and its right edge is ragged. Equal heights
         and a flush right edge are not both achievable without cropping the portraits
         to a common aspect ratio. (A spacer panel between Axel and Ben can force the
         flush edge, since PreTeXt only ever splits leftover space into equal gaps —
         tried and rejected, it left too wide a channel mid-row.) -->
